@bank all
// Writer 4, batch 4. Tiles talk (claude/tiles, section 23): what your opponent says over the board. tiles.start
// (a game begins), tiles.dock (they dock a three), tiles.miss (you missed a dock they saw), tiles.win (THEY win),
// tiles.lose (you beat them). Bubbles, 60 characters. Friendly: no gloating at you; losing is gracious or comic.
// trait: variants for competitive, chatty, shy, cheerful ("dry humour" has a space, so trait: can't reach it yet).

== tiles.start
- {hi}. Your move.
- Right. Let's see what you've got.
- Best of one? Best of one.
- I'll go easy. No, I won't. Your move.   #funny
- Tea's poured. Board's set. Off you go.
- Lovely. I've been wanting a game.
- Mind the corners. That's all I'll say.
- Go on, then. I'm ready.
? trait:competitive
- I don't play for fun. Well. Mostly for fun.   #funny
- Fair warning: I keep score.   #funny
? trait:chatty
- Oh good, a game. Did I tell you about my week?   #funny
- Right, so, Tiles. I love Tiles. Your move.
? trait:shy
- Oh. A game? All right. Yes. You first.
? trait:cheerful
- Brilliant! A game! Your move, {nick}.

== tiles.dock
- Docked.
- That's three.
- There we go.
- Oh, that's nice. That's three.
- Three in. Lovely.
- Sorry. Not sorry. Docked.   #funny
- Didn't see that coming, did you? Neither did I.   #funny
- One more for me.
? trait:competitive
- Three. Write it down.   #funny
- And that's how it's done.
? trait:chatty
- Ooh, look at that! Three! Look!
? trait:shy
- Oh. That docked. Sorry.
? trait:cheerful
- Ha! Three! I love this game.

== tiles.miss
- Ooh. You could have docked there.
- That was a three, just there. Next time.
- Don't look now, but you missed one.   #funny
- Close. There was a dock by the corner.
- Shh. I didn't see that. I saw that.   #funny
- Look left next time. Just saying.
? trait:competitive
- I'll take that dock, then. Thank you.   #funny
? trait:chatty
- Oh, you nearly had one! Just there! Never mind.
? trait:shy
- Um. There was a three. Sorry. Just there.
? trait:cheerful
- So close! You'll have it next go.

== tiles.win
- Good game.
- Close one. Really close.
- Good game. Again sometime?
- I got lucky with that last three.
- You'll have me next time. You nearly did.
- Thanks for the game. That was fun.
- Phew. That was a fight. Good game.
- Shake? Good game, {nick}.
? trait:competitive
- Good game. Rematch whenever you like.
? trait:chatty
- I won! I never win! Well, sometimes. Today!   #funny
? trait:shy
- Oh. I won? Sorry. It was close.
? trait:cheerful
- That was lovely. Again? Let's go again.

== tiles.lose
- Well played.
- You got me. Fair and square.
- Good game. You earned that one.
- Oh, that's me done. Well played.
- Beaten. Lovely. I mean it. Well, nearly.   #funny
- I'll get you next time. Good game.
- Where did you learn that? Well played.
- You're getting good at this. Too good.   #funny
? trait:competitive
- Again. Best of three. Starting now.   #funny
- Hm. Well played. I'm writing that down.
? trait:chatty
- You're a natural! I knew it! Did I teach you that?   #funny
? trait:shy
- Oh, well done. Really. That was good.
? trait:cheerful
- Ha! Beaten! Brilliant. Well played.
